{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwuqsDufAmPcgtoBRSMD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The ATT estimate is about 0.093. This is the propensity-score (inverse-odds) weighting estimate. Here `y` is binary (employed or not), so the effect is a difference in employment probability.\n\n- **Method:** I fit a logistic regression of `t` on x0–x16. I then reweighted the control group by p/(1−p) to resemble the treated group, and took the difference in mean `y` between the treated and the reweighted controls.\n- **Raw comparison:** The unadjusted difference is negative (0.779 treated vs 0.858 control), so the covariate adjustment changes the sign.\n- **Other adjusted estimates:** Two regression-based estimates came out lower. A linear regression with the covariates gives 0.081. An outcome model fit on controls only and applied to the treated gives 0.084. All three adjusted estimates agree on a positive effect of roughly 0.08 to 0.09.\n\nANSWER: 0.093"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":386,"cache_read_input_tokens":31602,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":386},"output_tokens":310,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4e86b3f-d5ef-4b6f-aa94-cc2ed9af3cec","uuid":"b040d26b-5fbf-4760-a0fe-9d5d7470c9a4","timestamp":"2026-11-11T22:14:58.566Z","request_id":"req_011CgwuqrzGUuhXGKKazDskS"}
